Z||000000||RiceCooker||08-28-2000||09:47 AM||||All went well with changing the water pump, no leaks except, I have a piercing squeal!<BR>I put on a brand new belt. The sound gets worse when i rev the car. it's unbearable even at 3000. <BR>Did i tension the belt too much?<BR>has anyone had this happen?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||08-28-2000||10:08 AM||||squalling belts are loose most times. You may have gotten oil or coolant on the pulleys which will also screw up the belt. Coolant has lubricant in it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RiceCooker||08-28-2000||11:23 AM||||The problem is that i can't even rotate the belt by turning the water pump pulley. I could before i did the switch, so i think it's too tight.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-28-2000||01:11 PM||||If you got it that tight it might not be the belt squalling. may be a bearing in one of the things the belt drives.||||reg||1
Z||000004||RiceCooker||08-28-2000||01:17 PM||||Yeah, i think so<BR>I'm gonna check it out tonight<P>P.S. taking the bus/train to work stinks!||||reg||1
