Z||000009||Master_Sushi||08-29-2000||12:07 PM||||My belt has been doing the same thing recently, but only when my fieros left outside overnight. I jsut went out and got a can of spray "belt dressing". I sprayed this on the belt and it got rid of the noise.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Im sure this is a somewhat temporary fix though. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I just have to get around to replacing the belt, and a few other things im sure. But it Sure looks hard to replace the belt on a Duke. I could barley spray the belt treatment on it. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||08-29-2000||12:23 PM||||The problem may be dew on the belt. The dressign would help keep that off. It's still likely a temporary fix. If the belt slips for any reason it wears fast.<P>The main V belt isn't too bad. It's tensioned by the alternator. It's the AC belt that's a pain for every one. (One of the other advantages to Serpent on the 87+ 4cyl.... Only one belt.)||||reg||1
